# Daybound's "if it is night, this permanent enters transformed" is a static ability of the permanent (CR 702.145b), and which
# replacement effects modify how a permanent enters is judged on it as it would exist on the battlefield (CR 614.12: "taking
# into account ... continuous effects that already exist and would apply to the permanent"). Under Humility ("All creatures
# lose all abilities") an Outland Liberator would have no daybound there, so cast at night it enters front face up (KI-59).
# The first Liberator, cast on turn 1 before Humility, makes it day (CR 702.145d); Bot2 casts nothing on turn 2, so turn 3 is
# night and that Liberator is Frenzied Trapbreaker (the positive control of "enters transformed" is
# day-and-night-swap-with-the-spells-cast-and-a-daybound-card-enters-transformed-at-night). On turn 3 Bot1 casts Humility,
# then the second Liberator at night: an Outland Liberator, a 1/1 with no keyword. It stays night all turn (the spells of a
# turn change it only at the next untap step, CR 731.2).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Outland Liberator
Plains
Humility
Outland Liberator
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

